Relevant columns & their usage
• sample_info.Sample  : primary key to join with the variant call_set_name  
• sample_info.Super_Population : separates “EAS” (cases) from all others (controls)  
• variants.reference_name   : chromosome name – filter = '12'  
• variants.start / variants.end : genomic co‑ordinates to return  
• variants.call.call_set_name  : sample ID inside every variant  
• variants.call.genotype    : ARRAY with 0 (=ref), 1 (=alt), -1 (=missing) – count alleles  
(we only need the first allele index; un‑nest both positions to count every allele)

Typical conditions  
• WHERE v.reference_name = '12'  
• CASE WHEN Super_Population = 'EAS' THEN 'EAS' ELSE 'OTHER' END AS grp  
• Only keep genotype values IN (0,1)  
• Aggregate counts by (grp, allele)  
• Expected counts of every cell ≥ 5  
• χ²Yates ≥ 29.71679  

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Below are ten exploratory → production BigQuery statements – each different – showing how to walk from a simple peek at the data to the final answer.  

```sql
